<%@ Page Title="Supplier Network" Language="C#" MasterPageFile="~/MasterPages/Site.Master" %>
<asp:Content ID="Content1" ContentPlaceHolderID="MainContent" runat="server">
<section class="public-page"><div class="public-hero"><div class="site-container"><span class="public-kicker"><i class="fa-solid fa-building"></i> Supplier discovery</span><h1>Compare supplier options before you <span>send the request.</span></h1><p>The supplier experience is designed to help factories review relevant procurement information in one place instead of calling multiple vendors without a consistent comparison.</p><div class="public-actions"><a class="public-button" href="~/Account/Register.aspx" runat="server">Register as a Portal User</a></div></div></div>
<section class="public-section"><div class="site-container"><div class="public-section-head"><span class="public-kicker">Comparison factors</span><h2>What can be compared?</h2><p>These are the information categories the future supplier workflow can organize.</p></div><div class="public-grid"><article class="public-card"><div class="public-icon"><i class="fa-solid fa-location-dot"></i></div><h3>Location</h3><p>Review supplier location and proximity to the requesting industrial plant.</p></article><article class="public-card"><div class="public-icon"><i class="fa-solid fa-boxes-stacked"></i></div><h3>Stock availability</h3><p>Review whether the requested part is represented as available in supplier inventory.</p></article><article class="public-card"><div class="public-icon"><i class="fa-solid fa-indian-rupee-sign"></i></div><h3>Price</h3><p>Compare indicative prices and quotation responses using Indian currency formatting.</p></article><article class="public-card"><div class="public-icon"><i class="fa-solid fa-file-invoice"></i></div><h3>Quotation response</h3><p>Collect supplier responses against a structured quotation request.</p></article><article class="public-card"><div class="public-icon"><i class="fa-solid fa-clock"></i></div><h3>Response status</h3><p>Keep procurement teams informed about request and response progress.</p></article><article class="public-card"><div class="public-icon"><i class="fa-solid fa-chart-simple"></i></div><h3>Decision support</h3><p>Present comparable information so the buyer can make a more informed selection.</p></article></div></div></section>
<section class="public-section alt"><div class="site-container"><div class="public-note"><strong>Demo information:</strong> supplier names, inventory values, prices and status values shown on the visitor pages are sample data for the MCA project interface. They are not claims about real businesses or inventory.</div></div></section></section>
</asp:Content>